# Skipped by Claude Code's Grep, Glob and file picker (they run on ripgrep, which reads
# .ignore next to .gitignore) and by editor searches that do the same. It hides files
# from SEARCH only: they can still be opened, and nothing else in the repo reads it.
#
# .gitignore already covers node_modules, built, output, web-ext-artifacts, logs,
# coverage, the vendored libraries and the e2e fixtures. This adds the files that are
# committed but only ever add noise to a search. Keep it in step with .claudeignore.

pnpm-lock.yaml

# Generated from chrome/_locales by localescript.mjs; every match here repeats one there.
combined-locales.json

*.map
*.min.js
*.min.css
